g no evidence ID, carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and is in any event inconsistent with a solo product.\n\nThe rider asks for escalation and I decline it, because no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare ledger; the timestamps agree and none run backwards; the trace is unimpaired; no exculpatory clause has been invoked against a missing or deficient artifact. EV-ADVIS-00713-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, but neither side asserts a traffic cause, so its absence is an uncited gap, not a POL-RD-10(5) trigger, and (as POL-RD-13 provides) it decides nothing. The two accounts are not mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength under POL-RD-10(7): the driver's own message and his statement agree the ride ended early; only his unweighted statement differs on fault. The suggestion that the distance_fare line of 9.35 does not reconcile with the 0.75 per-km rate does not meet POL-RD-10(8): it is a distance charge whose counterpart is the trip's own distance (6.8 km on the trip record, 6.83 km on the trace), an upfront decomposition is not required to reproduce per_km x km, and EV-FARE-00713 carries no admissibility issue. POL-RD-06 is not engaged either: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 250 completed trips, so no pattern, uplift or conduct referral is available.\n\nThe finding rests on EV-GPS-00713, EV-TRIP-00713 and EV-FARE-00713, all at weight 1.0; confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor. For the rider: the present state stands with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. If you believe the driver breached a solo booking or ended the trip without cause, that is a service-conduct matter this route-deviation policy does not monetise and this record does not prove. For the driver: the upfront fare stands and no compensation is awarded, as the billed distance (6.8 km) falls 0.03 km short of the trace (6.83 km), well under the 1.0 km POL-RD-04 threshold."
